    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d278-a5">

                <pb facs="0794" n="580" sameAs="frus:frus1871/pg580"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Sr. Don Francisco Alvarado to Mr. Henry Baxters </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 5.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Camayagua</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1871-05-24"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi>
                            24, 1871.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Esteemed sir</hi>: I officially ask protection of
                    your excellency for this city in case of its occupation by the troops of
                    Salvador, which is to be feared<hi rendition="#italic">;</hi> and as I do not
                    doubt that your excellency will be pleased to grant this protection, in virtue
                    of the guaranty of neutrality given by the United States of America, I beg you
                    to be pleased to inform me whether we may hoist the American flag in the public
                    square, as a sign of protection, on the entrance of the enemies and during their
                    stay in this capital.</p>
                <p>I subscribe myself your excellency’s most obedient servant.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>FRANCISCO ALVARADO.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
